cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Protein Label-Integrity Evaluation: Claude as a sequence/annotation consistency checker"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kim"
    given-names: "JangKeun"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0520-3703"
    affiliation: "Mason Lab, Weill Cornell Medicine"
year: 2026
repository-code: "https://github.com/jang1563/protein-label-integrity-eval"
abstract: >-
  A controlled evaluation showing that a prompted Claude model reliably detects
  when a protein's stored annotation does not match its sequence, including a
  hazardous sequence hidden under a benign-looking label, at about 100 percent
  sensitivity and 100 percent specificity on small adversarial panels and stable
  across five Claude versions. A defensive, model-agnostic label-integrity triage
  aid.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - biosecurity
  - label integrity
  - protein annotation
  - frontier model evaluation
  - Claude
license: "Apache-2.0"
